{"additions":225,"author":{"id":"U_kgDODt7pXw","is_bot":false,"login":"cmdr-chara","name":"Commander Chara"},"body":"# Objective\n\nI chose this issue because it was marked high severity.\n\nFixes #62760.\n\n## Solution\n\nBind generated `forwardPorts` mappings to `127.0.0.1` in Docker, Podman, and Compose. This includes service-qualified Compose ports and shared network namespaces. Explicit `appPort` and `runArgs` mappings keep their existing behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nI ran `cargo test --locked -p dev_container --lib forward_ports` locally on Linux: **5 passed, 0 failed**. The tests cover Docker and Podman command generation, preservation of explicit publications, Compose mappings and serialization, shared network namespaces, and empty or absent `forwardPorts`.\n\nWhitespace checks passed. The full library suite and live Docker/Podman/Compose smoke tests have not been run.\n\nScreenshot:\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1032\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b11b464-df83-4f37-b852-7df9078b1a6c\" />\n\nCode, tests, and description prepared with Codex assistance.\n\nRelease Notes:\n\n- Fixed dev container `forwardPorts` bindings to use IPv4 loopback instead of all host interfaces by default.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:12:57Z","deletions":1,"files":[{"path":"crates/dev_container/src/devcontainer_manifest.rs","additions":225,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"isDraft":false,"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAABgYGhPg","name":"cla-signed","description":"The user has signed the Contributor License Agreement","color":"ededed"},{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAABkklDwQ","name":"area:security & privacy","description":"Data privacy issue, security vulnerabilities, etc","color":"6C2950"},{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAACSvx30Q","name":"area:dev containers","description":"Feedback for Zed's dev containers feature","color":"2eaafb"}],"mergedAt":null,"number":63899,"reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","co